WEBVTT

00:36:26.833 --> 00:36:30.851
Do you seriously think
that I know the meaning of giving for you?

00:36:30.875 --> 00:36:32.143
AG: No.
EP: No.

00:36:32.167 --> 00:36:35.518
So it would be presumptuous for me
to just throw out a bunch of stuff.

00:36:35.542 --> 00:36:39.351
I have ideas, but we would be
discussing them together,

00:36:39.375 --> 00:36:42.018
and then I would ask you,
what do you think about that?

00:36:42.042 --> 00:36:44.351
Does that resonate for you?
Is that -- you know.

00:36:44.375 --> 00:36:46.559
And I think that's
a different conversation.

00:36:46.583 --> 00:36:48.143
AG: Yeah.

00:36:48.167 --> 00:36:51.184
EP: The solution -- I mean,
there's nothing to solve here

00:36:51.208 --> 00:36:53.726
unless you tell me, "I want to change it,"

00:36:53.750 --> 00:36:55.643
but that's not what you're telling me.

00:36:55.667 --> 00:36:57.226
Then there is nothing to solve.

00:36:57.250 --> 00:37:00.018
AG: OK, then my work is done, good.